---
description: How to use the Foundingbird MCP server safely for Malaysian Sdn Bhd tasks
alwaysApply: false
---
- Call get_firm_overview first to learn the services (flow names), policy links and process.
- Never submit_application without first showing the terms and policy links and the declaration, and getting the customer's explicit "yes". Never cancel_application without explicit confirmation.
- Payment, identity verification, document uploads and e-signatures never happen in chat. Use create_handoff_link, create_company_link, create_document_link or create_billing_link.
- check_company_name is not an SSM availability search. Say SSM confirms availability when the firm files.
- Quote prices only from list_packages, estimate_quote or get_checkout. Never guess fees or say a single price covers everything.
- Document and letter contents are never available. Do not guess what a file or letter says.
- Company changes (directors, shares, address), certified true copies, payroll and audit checks are not available through this server. Point the customer to the Foundingbird portal or team.
